  "returns": "record",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "published",
  "description_nl": "2026-10-11: s.115JB: when the tax on total income is less than 15% of the book profit (with surcharge 7% / 12% above 1 / 10 crore of book profit, marginal relief and 4% cess), that MAT is the tax; the excess over the normal tax becomes a credit (s.115JAA(1A)), carried 15 AYs. In a year the normal tax is more than MAT, credit is set off up to the difference (s.115JAA(4)). A company under 115BAA / 115BAB pays no MAT (s.115JB(5A)) and cannot use a credit (CBDT Circular 29/2019).",
